      "writtenOn": "2023-02-07T14:19:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do have to admit, this is giving me some pause.  Using the inline functions without the CONFIG enabled does improve code readability, but it also defines a set of functions we may never expect to be called, which runs directly counter to our code coverage goals.  I suppose we could label them uncoverable, but then if they do get put into the critical path in the future they do need to be tested.\n\nI don\u0027t have a great solution yet, beyond possibly going back to IS_ENABLED in front of calls we expect to be unreachable and removing those inline definitions.",
      "parentUuid": "0e8469b4_6dc1ca1a",
      "revId": "d1ed795d7e8356cfe3263ccf517139438e18706f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a44bb4de_8c7cb88d",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/drivers/ap_vdm_control/src/ap_vdm_control.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 802,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-07T16:46:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it goes against our coverage goals as long as they\u0027re covered, and they should be trivial to unit test (assuming we get that working). We do expect `dp_init` to be called when DP support is disabled in production, and I suspect we\u0027ll end up with a few more functions like that.\n\nWe might be able to reduce the need for them if we gave the alt mode modules a structured interface with thin wrappers like our drivers for TCPCs, etc. Then we could supply a null version of the structure for unsupported modes but still do a runtime nullness check before returning the default value. That would also require some DPM refactoring that should probably remain out of scope for this change.",
      "parentUuid": "4a0af440_cf4dd131",
      "revId": "d1ed795d7e8356cfe3263ccf517139438e18706f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
