      "writtenOn": "2023-02-07T17:20:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, now that you\u0027ve both +2\u0027d it, I\u0027ve talked myself into re-doing the mode entry host command which was providing coverage for a couple of the stubs.  It will now return an error for our use-case, which makes practical sense.  I\u0027ll optimistically hit CQ+1, but I suspect the stub coverage will regress enough that I need to figure out another approach. \n\nWhat do you view the as trivial approach to coverage?\n\nI agree that moving to a structured interface would remove the need to cover the functions, and also that I have a sufficient level of refactoring going on already without going for that.",
      "parentUuid": "a44bb4de_8c7cb88d",
